  "finding": "Weight-orthogonalizing mlp.down_proj at 25 layers (4-28) still left CLMI (mean_pool, full-stack probe) at 1.0 for the targeted concept. Root cause identified: projecting a single weight matrix (down_proj) to be orthogonal to direction d only prevents THAT matrix from adding NEW component along d -- it does nothing to remove a component along d already present in the residual stream from token embeddings or attention output (o_proj), neither of which this edit touches. Since contrastive prompts contain the concept name as literal tokens, the embedding layer alone likely injects most of the separable signal, which then propagates via the residual skip-connections regardless of what the MLPs do. Necessary but not sufficient -- motivates activation-level ablation (removes the component from the actual residual-stream value at runtime, regardless of source) as the theoretically correct mechanism, tested next in ogda_activation_ablation.py."
